Track 1: Tin Roof Swallows Cassiopeia
- Story & Context: When the power grid collapsed across the Vedado district during the equinox of 1998, projectionist Ismael hauled an unspooled canister of blank film up to the cinema roof, threading it through a hand-cranked lens while the heat made the tar paper stick to his bare soles. As the blank beam illuminated a bedsheet flapping in the trade winds, the crowd below mistook the flickering dust specks for shooting stars, screaming in joy when the flute entered with an ear-splitting, overblown trill that cut through the thunderous double-bass kick drum. Belén leaned over the parapet, her operatic cry cutting through the smell of burning transformer oil and blooming jasmine, singing "We loaded blank reels just to make the sky confess."
