Track 2: Sister Mirella’s Cardboard Sextant
- Story & Context: In the stifling projection booth of Cine Astral, Sister Mirella spent thirty years slicing forbidden romantic dialogue out of church-banned imports, hoarding the discarded acetate strips in empty mango crates until her fingers smelled permanently of vinegar and ripe fruit. On her final evening before eviction, she mapped Venus using a homemade telescope fashioned from a mailing tube, confessing to Ismael that every silent reel she ever ran was silently dedicated to the sailor who taught her how to hold a flute. The track captures her whispered confession over a lazy, syncopated Rhodes chord sequence that suddenly fractures into a bone-rattling symphonic breakdown, as Belén belts, "I cut out every kiss so they would belong to me."
